"bd close claude-guard-7dn --reason=\"Answered live 2026-09-05. PermissionDenied does NOT fire when the user clicks deny in the dialog; only PermissionRequest fired (no tool_use_id). The click IS recorded in the Claude Code transcript at transcript_path: a user-type line whose message.content has a tool_result {tool_use_id, is_error: true, content: 'The user doesn't want to proceed with this tool use...'} and toolUseResult: 'User rejected tool use'. So the guard can learn the answer by reading the transcript for the tool_use_id from its own pre_tool_use record. Transcript format is undocumented.\" 2>&1 | head -1\nbd update claude-guard-2mb --notes=\"Design input from claude-guard-7dn (2026-09-05): the user's dialog answer is only visible in the transcript JSONL (transcript_path in every payload), keyed by tool_use_id, as toolUseResult 'User rejected tool use' with is_error true. An allow shows as a normal tool_result plus a PostToolUse record. So the 5 minute memory reads: for prior pre_tool_use records with the same subject in this session, look up their tool_use_id in the transcript; rejected within 5 min => deny, allowed within 5 min => allow?, else deny-first. Transcript is undocumented: parse leniently, fail open.\" 2>&1 | head -1"
