"bd remember --key ghostty-native-tabs-ax \"Measured 2026-09-05 against Ghostty (native macOS window tabs). (1) window_dump: AXWindows lists exactly one AXStandardWindow, the selected tab; hidden tabs are separate NSWindows with their own CGWindowIDs but are not exposed over AX. (2) App log with the observer watching pid 1042: a tab switch fires NO notification the observer subscribes to (no AXWindowCreated, no AXUIElementDestroyed, no AXFocusedWindowChanged reached the callback). The new tab is first seen by the session-open reconcile (~15 ms after 'session opened', inside the 125 ms show delay), where front_focused_window tags it focused, and the old tab is reported 'known window not in the AX pass; closing'. Handling: WatchEvent::Opened{focused} -> WindowOpened then WindowFocused; Engine::promote_in_session moves a mid-session focus to the head of the session list keeping the highlight; switcher sets origin. RUST_LOG=windough_mac=trace logs every AX notification before filtering, to check whether Ghostty sends anything at all on a tab switch.\" 2>&1 | tail -1; jj status | head -8"
"bd remember --key ghostty-native-tabs-ax \"Measured 2026-09-05 against Ghostty (native macOS window tabs). (1) window_dump: AXWindows lists exactly one AXStandardWindow, the selected tab; hidden tabs are separate NSWindows with their own CGWindowIDs but are not exposed over AX. (2) RUST_LOG=windough_mac=trace (logs every AX notification before filtering): a tab switch sends ONLY a burst of 7 AXTitleChanged notifications carrying the incoming tab's window id. No AXFocusedWindowChanged, no AXWindowCreated, no AXUIElementDestroyed. The old tab is first found gone by the next session-open reconcile ('known window not in the AX pass; closing'). Handling: observer::discover turns any notification for an unknown window into WatchEvent::Opened{focused: is_front_focused}; switcher feeds WindowOpened then WindowFocused; Engine::promote_in_session heads the session list for a mid-session focus (backstop for reconcile-first discovery, ~15 ms after session open, inside the 125 ms show delay).\" 2>&1 | tail -1"
"bd remember --key ghostty-native-tabs-ax \"Measured 2026-09-05 against Ghostty (native macOS window tabs). (1) window_dump: AXWindows lists exactly one AXStandardWindow, the selected tab; hidden tabs are separate NSWindows with their own CGWindowIDs but are not exposed over AX. (2) RUST_LOG=windough_mac=trace (logs every AX notification before filtering): a tab switch sends ONLY a burst of 7 AXTitleChanged notifications, each from a different CHILD element inside the incoming tab's window (never the window element, so AXSubrole checks and CFEqual against the window element both miss; _AXUIElementGetWindow on the child still yields the window id). No AXFocusedWindowChanged, no AXWindowCreated, no AXUIElementDestroyed. The old tab is first found gone by the next session-open reconcile. Handling: the title branch resolves the element via kAXWindowAttribute and matches known windows by id; observer::discover turns a notification for an unknown window into WatchEvent::Opened{focused: is_front_focused}; verified in the log: discovery fires ~1-2 ms after the first title notification, before ⌘Tab, with focused=true. Engine::promote_in_session remains as a backstop for reconcile-first discovery.\" 2>&1 | tail -1; cargo fmt --check && cargo nextest run 2>&1 | rg \"Summary\"; cargo clippy --all-targets 2>&1 | rg -n \"^(warning|error)\" | rg -v \"future version\" | head; jj status | head -8"
"bd remember --key ghostty-native-tabs-ax \"Measured 2026-09-05 with crates/windough-mac/examples/window_dump against Ghostty (native macOS window tabs, several tabs open): AXWindows lists exactly one AXStandardWindow, the selected tab. Hidden tabs are separate NSWindows with their own CGWindowIDs but are not exposed over AX. A tab switch is therefore seen as one window destroyed and one created; the created window is already the frontmost app's focused window, which is why WatchEvent::Opened carries a focused flag and the switcher feeds WindowFocused after WindowOpened. Not yet measured: the exact order of AXFocusedWindowChanged vs AXWindowCreated on a tab switch (run destroy_probe against Ghostty's pid and switch tabs).\" 2>&1 | tail -3"
"bd remember --key ghostty-native-tabs-ax \"Measured 2026-09-05 with crates/windough-mac/examples/window_dump against Ghostty (native macOS window tabs, several tabs open): AXWindows lists exactly one AXStandardWindow, the selected tab. Hidden tabs are separate NSWindows with their own CGWindowIDs but are not exposed over AX. A tab switch is therefore seen as one window destroyed and one created; the created window is already the frontmost app's focused window, which is why WatchEvent::Opened carries a focused flag and the switcher feeds WindowFocused after WindowOpened. Not yet measured: the exact order of AXFocusedWindowChanged vs AXWindowCreated on a tab switch (run destroy_probe against Ghostty's pid and switch tabs).\" 2>&1 | tail -3; git status --short"
"bd update claude-guard-0lm --notes=\"Live logs 2026-09-05 (165 Bash calls): the interpreters Claude actually uses are nu -c '...' (multi-line scripts, several per session) and python3 -c \\\"...\\\", far more than sh -c. nu is not bash, so the most the guard can do is a Warn naming it as uninspected, like \\$(...). python3 -c is the same. bash -c and sh -c can be re-segmented. Newline-separated command lists are already split by the segmenter (50 of 165 calls had newlines, 0 parse errors).\" 2>&1 | head -1"
"bd update claude-guard-110 --description=\"Rules become a file, not Rust const data. Policies, not programs: closed, total, typed at load, s-expression syntax with bracket term patterns. Design: docs/design/rule-language/01-decisions.md (D1-D18) and 02-principles.md (16 principles). FIRST VERSION (this bead): encode the current Rust rule table and nothing else; the guard loads the shipped file and every existing test passes with the same wire output. In: ordered deny/ask/warn rows with reason and instead; Bash patterns with the current tokens in bracket syntax; variables; predicates ancestor-has, under, and, or, not; tool patterns for Write and Edit; loader with embedded file, optional user file, positioned type errors, fail-open on a bad file; check forms for matcher and evaluator; rules --export; delete rules.rs table. Out (later beads): extern (D9), fact lifetimes (D8), cwd tracking (D13), unknown and evidence (D10, D14), history and sequence patterns (D17, claude-guard-dvs), read freshness (D16, claude-guard-j4t).\""
"bd update claude-guard-1ma --description=\"Design: D22-D27 in docs/design/rule-language/01-decisions.md (2026-09-06). Elaborator returns {cmd, options: [{text, flags, value?}], args, inner?}; partition property, round-trip over the log corpus; data in the rule language with extern escape hatch; getopt clustering; tokens keep their meaning; inner set ships built in (sudo env nice nohup timeout xargs ssh bash sh nu python3); claude-guard commands (log review: calls, generic-row hits, flagged calls, status, carapace availability) and claude-guard commands add <name> (carapace export to ~/.config/claude-guard/commands/<name>.scm); additive loading by name. Supersedes claude-guard-dvd, claude-guard-3ev, claude-guard-0lm.\" && bd close claude-guard-dvd claude-guard-3ev claude-guard-0lm --reason=\"Superseded by the command elaborator design, claude-guard-1ma (D22-D27): inner declarations cover ssh, the wrappers, and the -c shells with one mechanism.\""
"bd update claude-guard-1ma --notes=\"Jake, 2026-09-06: elaboration does not change the meaning of -... or ... or *, ONLY what they match on. The tokens keep their semantics; the elaborated word list is the input, where an option word for a declared command is the flag together with its value because the arity is known. Write D23 in those words.\""
"bd update claude-guard-2mb --description=\"SUPERSEDED IN SHAPE by the rule language (claude-guard-110, D17): escalation and the dialog memory become history primitives, (denied-this :within D) and (user-denied-this :within D), read from the session log and the Claude Code transcript, with their rules in the shipped rule file. The rm rule uses (session-created <path>) over the log. Keep the transcript-reading design from the original description: a user-type line whose tool_result has is_error true and toolUseResult 'User rejected tool use', keyed by tool_use_id; parse leniently, fail open. Original: repeat deny becomes ask; 5 minute memory of the user's dialog answer, session-scoped; rm rule (recursive rm passes only for dirs created this session, else ask).\" && bd dep add claude-guard-2mb claude-guard-110"
"bd update claude-guard-520 --design=\"Plan as of 2026-09-05, deferred by Jake. On jj describe/commit/new with -m or --message: allow when the message has a conventional prefix (feat fix docs chore refactor config new test perf build ci style revert, optional (scope), optional !, then ': ') and no attribution (Co-Authored-By, Claude-Session, Generated with, created with Claude, bare Claude/Anthropic, case-insensitive); deny otherwise with the failed check in the reason; subject over 72 chars denied. Needs Decision::Allow { context } (first allow; spec non-goal lifted) and a Subject::Flag { command pattern, flags } that extracts the value after -m or --message=; Guidance gains a computed variant. No -m => no opinion. git commit untouched (git-in-jj covers it). Tests: each prefix, scope, !, each marker, long subject, --message= form, quoting styles, multi-line body, allow wire format byte-exact.\" 2>&1 | head -1"
"bd update claude-guard-6tq --claim 2>&1 | head -1"
"bd update claude-guard-7dn --notes=\"2026-09-05 live capture. PermissionRequest payload keys: cwd, effort{level}, hook_event_name, permission_mode (was 'auto'), permission_suggestions[], prompt_id, scratchpad_dir, session_id, tool_input, tool_name, transcript_path. NO tool_use_id, so Option was right. PermissionDenied: not yet captured; needs Jake to click deny in a dialog.\" 2>&1 | head -1\nbd update claude-guard-h50 --notes=\"2026-09-05 live capture. SessionStart payload: source (startup|resume|...), session_title ('Building Claude Guard'), context_tokens, seconds_since_last_response, estimated_cache_write_usd, prompt_cache_likely_expired, scratchpad_dir, transcript_path, cwd. SessionEnd payload: reason ('prompt_input_exit'), prompt_id, cwd, transcript_path. session_title is the natural label for the review UI's session list.\" 2>&1 | head -1\nbd update claude-guard-6o4 --notes=\"2026-09-05: no subagent ran in the first live sessions; agent_id was null on all 14 records. Still open.\" 2>&1 | head -1\nbd update claude-guard-zjr --notes=\"2026-09-05 live: MCP server ids can be UUIDs for claude.ai connectors, e.g. mcp__84bb71d3-27ea-4b3e-807d-efd31ca696c7__search_cloudflare_documentation. A server facet needs a display-name mapping or it shows UUIDs.\" 2>&1 | head -1\nbd remember \"claude-guard hook payloads, captured live 2026-09-05: PostToolUse adds duration_ms, effort, tool_response; Bash tool_response = {stdout, stderr, interrupted, isImage, noOutputExpected}. PermissionRequest has no tool_use_id. SessionStart carries session_title and source; SessionEnd carries reason. One 30-minute session with PostToolUse registered wrote 510 KB.\" 2>&1 | head -1"
"bd update claude-guard-8x3 --notes=\"Architecture section should explain the three truth values and Kleene's tables (three-valued logic, from Kleene 1938; SQL NULL uses the same tables): false AND unknown is false, true OR unknown is true, every other combination with unknown stays unknown, NOT leaves unknown alone. Say why it matters here: a timed-out extern in an (and ...) never becomes a silent pass; D14 turns unknown on a matched pattern into an ask. Jake asked for this on 2026-09-06 after reading step 3.\" && bd show claude-guard-8x3 | head -5"
"bd update claude-guard-948 --notes=\"rm design agreed in principle 2026-09-05: rm without -r/-R/-rf passes. Recursive rm: if every literal target is under a directory this session created (a passed mkdir subject or a Write/Edit path earlier in the same session log), allow with a context line; otherwise ask, naming the target. Dynamic targets always ask. Reads the session log like escalation, so build it with claude-guard-2mb. Jake's Bash(rm *) ask entry stays until then.\" 2>&1 | head -1; bd dep add claude-guard-948 claude-guard-2mb 2>&1 | head -1"
"bd update claude-guard-j4t --description=\"Record mtime and size of every file a Read, Write, or Edit touched at PostToolUse. Predicates (has-read <path>) and (read-fresh <path>); the second holds only when recorded mtime and size match the file now. Scope is the SESSION: a read from an earlier session does not count, because the context that read it is gone. Open: whether a subagent's read counts for the parent (waits on claude-guard-6o4). Target rule: deny writes to an existing file that is not read-fresh, including Bash redirects and tee, with the last read time in the reason. Design: docs/design/rule-language/01-decisions.md D16. Depends on the rule language (claude-guard-110).\""
"bd update homelab-boq --title \"Delete stale _acme-challenge.stats.home.cipher.cc TXT (manually, not via tofu)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; bd comments add homelab-boq \"Correction 2026-09-05: NOT imported after all. _acme-challenge.* TXT records are transient, created and deleted by Caddy's DNS-01 flow; if tofu held one it would recreate the dead token after every renewal. scripts/cf-module-gen.nu now skips them as a class (not-ours) and notes the skip in the zone map. This one is a leftover from an interrupted renewal: delete it in the Cloudflare dashboard (cipher.cc > DNS) or with a one-off DELETE /zones/:id/dns_records/:id using an edit token. Nothing depends on it.\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"bead updated\""
