"cd /Users/jakes/code/personal/jakes/.homelab\njj describe -m \"fix(runners): run macOS under launchd, declare both runner identities\n\nJobs on jakes-m4x hung at 'Complete job' until the daemon was killed, at which\npoint they went green. The cause was SIGTTIN, not the runner. The daemon ran in\nthe foreground from a terminal, so job children inherited the controlling\nterminal while sitting outside the foreground process group; the first one to\ntouch the tty was stopped by the kernel and never resumed, and the runner waited\non it forever. Killing the daemon killed the stopped child, teardown finished,\nand the result posted. Confirmed with ps: dist/save.js in STAT=T at zero CPU.\n\nUpgrading forgejo-runner 12.13.2 to 13.1.0 did not fix it on its own, despite\nthat release shipping a host-executor TTY fix. macOS has no setsid, so launchd\nis the only native way to run without a controlling terminal. The daemon is now\nlaunchd.daemons.forgejo-runner with RunAtLoad and KeepAlive both false: activation\nregisters it without running it, and starting it stays a deliberate act.\n\nBoth runners also stop registering. Forgejo 15 removed registration tokens, so\neach now declares a uuid and secret through settings.server.connections. On the\nNAS that meant dropping the module's ExecStartPre, which deleted .runner before\ncalling a register command the server no longer answers, so any label change\nwould have destroyed a working runner and failed to rebuild it. The stale\n.runner had to be deleted once by hand; declared mode never writes one.\n\nPutting the identity in config.yaml rather than in --uuid/--token-url flags is\nwhat let run.sh go away entirely, since launchd's ProgramArguments then needs no\nshell to interpolate anything. EnvironmentVariables replaces the env -i trick\ndeclaratively, and the job PATH is unchanged: the toolchain buildEnv hashes to\nthe same store path it did before the move.\n\ntailcat is in this commit because the input bump forces it. Upstream moved\n--allow from a global flag onto the serve subcommand, so the old invocation dies\nat startup with a parse error, and it fails at runtime rather than at build time.\nIts test suite also does not survive a many-core Linux sandbox, failing with\n'text file busy' as the harness execs a binary it still holds open for writing;\nthe same rev builds clean on aarch64-darwin with checks enabled, so doCheck is\noff with a note to retry it on the next bump. Splitting these hunks out would\nleave an intermediate commit that does not run.\n\nThe macos-ci nix profile and packages.macos-ci-toolchain are gone: the darwin\ngeneration is a GC root, so the profile bought nothing once launchd was doing\nthe launching. Removing it produced a byte-identical darwin store path.\n\njust runner-start now uses just's [continue] attribute with an && runner-stop\ndependency instead of a hand-rolled trap. [continue] only proceeds when the body\nexits successfully, so a trap converts Ctrl-C into a clean exit. runner-stop\nverifies the daemon actually died rather than assuming it: an earlier version of\nthis recipe silently leaked a runner that kept polling for ten minutes.\" 2>&1 | tail -3"
