"jj describe -m \"fix: a window discovered focused in the frontmost app ranks first, so native tab switches keep their app at the front\n\nNative tabs are separate windows. Measured 2026-09-05 with window_dump:\nGhostty with several tabs reports exactly one AXStandardWindow, the\nselected tab. A tab switch therefore destroys one window and creates\nanother, and the created one was pushed to the back of the MRU while the\nfocus event for it was dropped as unknown. Ghostty lost its rank on every\ntab switch.\n\nWatchEvent::Opened now carries a focused flag: the window is the focused\nwindow of the frontmost app at discovery. The created callback reads it\nvia is_front_focused; the background per-app pass reads it via\nfront_focused_window so the main thread makes no extra AX call. The\nswitcher feeds WindowFocused after WindowOpened when the flag is set,\nmid-session included, since peek never creates windows and the next quick\n⌘Tab must lead back to the tab the user was in.\" && jj new && jj log -r '@-' --no-graph -T 'change_id.short() ++ \" \" ++ description.first_line() ++ \"\\n\"'"
"jj describe -m \"fix: learn a Ghostty tab switch from its title burst, and head the session list with a late focused discovery\n\nMeasured 2026-09-05 with RUST_LOG=windough_mac=trace, which now logs every\nAX notification before filtering: a Ghostty tab switch sends only a burst\nof seven AXTitleChanged, each from a child element inside the incoming\ntab's window, never the window element. No focus change, no created, no\ndestroyed. The watcher matched title changes by window-element identity\nand dropped them for unknown windows, so the only live signal a tab switch\ngives was thrown away. The new tab was first seen by the session-open\nreconcile, ~15 ms after ⌘Tab, and appended to the bottom of the list the\nsession had already snapshotted.\n\nObserver: a title change resolves its element to the enclosing window via\nAXWindow and matches known windows by id. A notification for an unknown\nwindow is a discovery: the window is read and reported opened, tagged\nfocused when the app is frontmost with that window focused. Focus\nnotifications for unknown windows take the same path. Verified in the\nlog: discovery lands 1-2 ms after the first title notification, before\n⌘Tab, and the reconcile then reports only the old tab closing.\n\nEngine: a focus that arrives mid-session moves the window to the head of\nthe session list with the highlight kept on the same window. Kept as the\nbackstop for any app whose window is still first found by the reconcile,\nwhich lands inside the 125 ms show delay. The switcher makes such a\nwindow the session origin when peek has not moved anything yet.\n\nDebug lines for reconcile-driven closes, unfocused opens, and rejected\ndiscoveries, so the next silent miss shows up in the log.\" && jj new && jj log -r '@-' --no-graph -T 'change_id.short() ++ \" \" ++ description.first_line() ++ \"\\n\"'"
