"jj split --no-pager -m \"feat(cloudflare): import the account into OpenTofu as a generated module\n\nPhase 1 of homelab-3dp, applied: 317 resources adopted into Garage state with\nzero diff, confirmation plan reads No changes.\n\ncloudflare/ mirrors dns/: one locals map per zone (type, DNSSEC, setting\noverrides, records, rulesets, email routing) in zone-<slug>.tf, parked zones\ntogether in zones-minor.tf, and one this resource per type keyed by path\n(zone_setting.this[\\\"cipher.cc/ssl\\\"], dns_record.this[\\\"cipher.cc/@/MX\\\"],\nruleset.this[\\\"cipher.cc/firewall\\\"]). Zone settings are a defaults table plus\noverrides; shared AnonAddy values live in shared.tf; the NAS tailnet address\ncomes from homelab.json, which nix now reads too (nix-inert: PURE).\n\nGenerated from a cf-terraforming sweep by scripts/cf-module-gen.nu; the sweep\nitself is scripts/cf-discover.nu (rate-limit aware, --retry, unavailable vs\nforbidden classification). docs/cloudflare-zone-settings.md lists every zone\nsetting with its live value and whether tofu manages it.\n\nLeft out on purpose, with reasons in the generator header: Cloudflare-owned\nrecords (Email Routing, Workers placeholders, ACME tokens), router-updated\ndynamic DNS records, settings at their defaults, bot_management and\nemail_routing_settings (5.24.0 provider cannot plan/read them cleanly),\nDNSSEC in pending, anything wrangler or the legal-docs infra owns.\n\nProvider 5.24.0 enabled; cloudflare_api_token defaults to null so the\nread-only token from a gitignored .env (just loads it) suffices for plan and\nthe import. Follow-ups: homelab-boq, homelab-qlo, homelab-7d5 (first edit-token\nchange), homelab-cl2, homelab-8cm, homelab-3ex, homelab-3j4, homelab-f12.\" 'all() ~ hosts/nas/modules/forgejo.nix ~ hosts/nas/modules/sops.nix' 2>&1 | tail -5; echo \"--- log:\"; jj log --no-pager -r '@-::@' 2>&1 | head -8; echo \"--- left in working copy:\"; jj status 2>&1 | head -6"
"jj split --no-pager -m \"fix(cloudflare): emit import blocks only on request after the first apply\n\nEverything is in state now, so a regenerated cloudflare-imports.tf would be\nnoise that has to be deleted before every commit. The generator writes it only\nwith --with-imports, the recipe formats it only if it exists, and the README\ndescribes the adopt-a-new-object flow instead of the first import.\n\n(The matching two-line change in the justfile is left in the working copy: it\nshares the file with in-flight Forgejo runner edits and cannot be split by path.)\" scripts/cf-module-gen.nu README.md 2>&1 | tail -4; echo \"--- log:\"; jj log --no-pager -r '@---::@' 2>&1 | head -10; echo \"--- working copy:\"; jj status 2>&1 | head -8"
